From 4dac1d9358a6d61706c2e31dae9e5e1f1e9750f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kuzma30 <kuzemkoa@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:09:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/24] Modeling Algorithms - Cut two fillets along their
 intersection at a corner

Two fillets ending at a vertex with more than three sharp edges were always
closed by a corner patch (PerformMoreThreeCorner). When the fillets have no
common support face and each support of one meets a support of the other
on an edge at the vertex (the bottom edges of a pocket wall and of the
cylinder next to it, both with a chamfer, FreeCAD issue 31894), the exact
corner is the intersection of the two fillets, from one of these edges to
the other. The patch there left gaps of 0.02 mm.

PerformTwoCornerMitre builds that corner. The traces of the fillets must
meet on both edges. A trace that has to go a little past the end of its
surfdata to reach the other fillet gets its surfdata extended there; the
existing part of the surface and of the trace keeps its parameters, and the
pcurves are the old ones followed by the projected new piece. The stripes
then end on the intersection curve. In any other configuration, or when
the intersection is poor (an extension too long to follow the fillet), it
returns false with nothing changed and the corner patch is built as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
